shot into space. It's like, of course. He didn't get a little sub and go underneath the ocean, you know, which is probably harder to do. He shot himself into space because he likes to be high above people. That's a deep universal. And he wanted attention. And boy, the powerful will go to no ends to be above people and to get a lot of attention. What a what a lampoonable waste of resources and opportunity. But just on a more quotidian level, I mean, if an average person thinks that he or she wants power, what's the best way to get more of it? It's interesting. There's there's work that shows like Cameron Anderson, my collaborator at Berkeley, has this nice finding. You know, you can study these groups. No one has a position of power. They just start doing something together.
射入太空。这就像，当然。他没有弄个小潜水艇潜入海底，你知道，这可能更难做到。他把自己射入太空，因为他喜欢高高在上。这是一个深刻的普遍现象。他想要关注。天哪，掌权者会不惜一切代价高高在上并获得大量关注。多么令人嘲讽的资源和机会的浪费。但只是在更日常的层面上，我的意思是，如果一个普通人认为他或她想要权力，获得更多权力的最好方法是什么？这很有趣。有，有研究表明，比如卡梅伦·安德森，我在伯克利的合作者，有这个很好的发现。你知道，你可以研究这些群体。没有人拥有权力职位。他们只是开始一起做某事。

45
00:28:09.000 --> 00:29:01.000
And they can figure out who rises. And there are things like speak up. And so one of the things I tell people as they adapt to leadership is like, make sure you voice yourself, right? Even if you're introverted, even if maybe you come from working in a gender biased context, like take the courage to speak up, connect to other people, ask great questions. propose bold ideas and be ready to back off them. And one of the, I think, motivations for me to write the power paradox and to do this work is it shows that, and also to remember how much of power and influence in the world is local and comes from unexpected people, right? The best-selling writer of all time is Agatha Christie, you know, no comparison.
他们可以弄清楚谁会崛起。有像大声说出来这样的事情。所以我告诉人们适应领导力时的一件事是，确保你表达自己，对吧？即使你内向，即使也许你来自性别偏见的环境，比如拿出勇气大声说出来，与他人联系，提出伟大的问题。提出大胆的想法并准备好退缩。我认为我写《权力悖论》并做这项工作的一个动机是它表明，也要记住世界上多少权力和影响力是局部的，来自意想不到的人，对吧？有史以来最畅销的作家是阿加莎·克里斯蒂，你知道，无法比较。

46
00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:51.000
I believe the most important technological innovation alongside the computer of the 20th century was the birth control pill. And that was led by Margaret Sanger, who's this kind of an unconventional person with no resources. You could go on it, Black Lives Matter, abolitionism, et cetera, were led by people who influenced locally through social networks, through courage. And so I think when we rethink power, and it's not just wealth or domination, or being a male, but it has this local quality to it. It gives us reason to go after it and for social good. So is being benevolent and cooperative than the best way to hang on to power once you get it?
我相信20世纪与计算机并列的最重要的技术创新是避孕药。这是由玛格丽特·桑格领导的，她是一个没有资源的非传统人物。你可以继续，黑人的命也是命，废奴主义等等，都是由通过社交网络、通过勇气在局部施加影响的人领导的。所以我认为当我们重新思考权力时，它不仅仅是财富或支配，或成为男性，但它具有这种局部性。它给了我们追求它并为了社会利益的理由。那么仁慈和合作是获得权力后保持权力的最好方法吗？

47
00:29:51.000 --> 00:30:27.000
Yeah, you know, people always press me on that. And I think there's a lot of neat new work by people like Rob Willer and economists, that, you know, sharing resources in a thoughtful way is a really good way to rise in social status, right? Building social ties is a good way to gain power. There's amazing social network research showing that if you can build a lot of strong ties with people where they like you and trust you in finance firms
是的，你知道，人们总是就此向我施压。我认为像罗伯·威勒和经济学家这样的人有很多很棒的新工作，即，以深思熟虑的方式分享资源是提升社会地位的好方法，对吧？建立社会联系是获得权力的好方法。有惊人的社交网络研究表明，如果你能与人们建立许多强大的联系，让他们喜欢你并信任你，在金融公司

48
00:30:27.000 --> 00:31:05.000
or tech firms, you'll have a lot of power because you're kind of in the mix and you're getting a lot of information. So that's all pro-social. But I also think, you know, you have to be ready to fight for stuff. You know, you have to be ready to call out the Machiavellian and to stand up for stuff and draw a hard line. So I'd say 75% in many of today's contexts that our audience might be working in is about connecting, empathizing, sharing. But be ready to fight for the things you believe in. Do the dynamics of power change within people as they age?
或科技公司，你将拥有很多权力，因为你处于混合状态，并且你获得了大量信息。所以这一切都是亲社会的。但我也认为，你知道，你必须准备好为事情而战。你知道，你必须准备好指出马基雅维利主义者，并为事情挺身而出，划定底线。所以我说在当今许多听众可能工作的环境中，75%是关于联系、共情、分享。但要准备好为你相信的事情而战。权力的动态会随着人们年龄的增长而改变吗？

