00:31:05.000 --> 00:31:42.000
So maybe kids who, you know, were powerful or even bullies, will they continue to be that way as adults? What does the trajectory look like through life? That's a question that we regrettably, psychological, developmental longitudinal studies are hard to do. You've got to follow people for 10 years. And in some sense, we don't have an answer to that question. And one of the critiques of a lot of the literature I'm citing is, like a lot of social psychology is it's atemporal. It studies people in one instant in time.
所以也许小时候，你知道，有权力的，甚至是恶霸，他们成年后会继续那样吗？生命轨迹看起来是什么样的？这是一个我们遗憾地，心理学、发展纵向研究很难做的问题。你必须跟踪人们10年。在某种意义上，我们没有那个问题的答案。我引用的许多文献的批评之一是，像很多社会心理学一样，它是无时间的。它在某一瞬间研究人们。

50
00:31:42.000 --> 00:32:22.000
